data namespace_kernel_authority_amendment_note: String = "THE KERNEL BAR AS FIRST WRITTEN DEADLOCKED ITS OWN SUCCESSOR, and this amendment is the fix (operator ruling, 2026-08-01). The recut landed namespace-binding-kernel with a red_control ending 'no second place in the compiler makes that same decision' and a handback demanding 'evidence that nothing else decides the same question'. That bar cannot be met while the bootstrap seed keeps its own hand-written none/one/many mirror inside the v1 adapter, and that mirror cannot be deleted until generic emission carries the canonical carrier with its required bounds. But namespace-reference-derived-closure DEPENDS on the kernel. So on the day the recut merged, the next step was already unstartable for a reason that had nothing to do with what the next step needs: deriving candidate populations does not require the seed mirror to be gone, it requires the canonical decision to EXIST and be callable.\n\nTHE CUT IS AUTHORITY VERSUS RETIREMENT. Owning the canonical decision and removing every rival implementation of it are separate achievements with separate evidence, and fusing them made an acceptance bar that no amount of correct kernel work could satisfy. The kernel now owns being the one canonical authority; namespace-legacy-choice-retirement owns deleting the older mechanisms, and the seed mirror is named there as one of its rows. A new node was deliberately NOT minted: that node already reads 'delete every other way of deciding what a name means' and already inventories every remaining place that decides, so the mirror is a row it should always have carried, and minting a sibling would have been a second home for one concept.\n\nTHE ADAPTER IS NOT THEREBY BLESSED. It remains a declared scaffold with its dissolution trigger on its own carrier, counted and visible; moving WHERE its retirement is tracked does not lower what is owed. What changes is only that a temporary bootstrap realization no longer gates work that does not depend on it.\n\nTWO ACCEPTANCE SENTENCES WERE ALSO WRONG AND ARE CORRECTED HERE. The red_control said 'a malformed name refuses', but this boundary accepts occurrence identities and derives no name spelling at all, so it named a check no implementation executes — it now reads malformed occurrence TRANSPORT. And the bar now states the two refusals that distinguish a malformed supplied population from a real verdict: a candidate handed in the wrong role refuses distinctly from one that is absent, and the same declaration supplied twice refuses as malformed rather than counting as two. Only two DISTINCT declaration identities are ambiguity. Collapsing either of those into an ordinary verdict would let a defective candidate producer read as a legitimate naming answer, which is the state-space conflation this whole lane exists to remove."

data five_minute_ci_gate_program_note: String = "PROGRAM BOUNDARY, NOT A SINGLE PR (operator dispatch K, 2026-08-01; sequence revision eager-boar-610, 2026-08-01; contract re-anchored by operator ruling 2026-08-02). Product contract: every required operation performs the bare minimum computation needed to serve it — no recomputation of any semantic fact whose inputs did not change; wall-clock falls out of the realization/materialization goals rather than defining them. Five minutes is NOT the contract — it is the distress ceiling ('this is hard / not working well'), retained only as the Stage C checkpoint bound. Sub-lane roster, revised by the CI2-0 STOP (operator ruling 2026-08-10, superseding the 2026-08-08 CI-0 recut) — UNORDERED: dispatch order follows the graph edges, and THE NATIVE ROW NO LONGER PRECEDES THIS GATE. That edge is deleted, on a measurement rather than a preference: a 3,290s floor carries 97s of witness evaluation, so an infinitely fast evaluator leaves ~97 percent of the floor standing and native execution cannot be this gate's prerequisite. The one-PR CI-0 shape is retired with it — #8043/#8080 attempted it, the cohort was empty at the real frontier, and native-selected-witness-bundle is re-cut as the named self-host frontier it always was. The lanes: #7522 warm-merge-admission with net wall receipt; #7534 continued as materialization substrate under module-grain (hierarchy: module parse/type/interface → resolved entry → native bundle; no default CI savings until ordinary invocations consume it); union CLOSED per #7533 → per-entry-assembly narrow lane; this parent registration. Native-at-small-scale evidence has LANDED; operational migration rate remains OPEN with equivalence/fallback/identity/memory fail-closed. The landed change, its merge commit, the head the witnesses actually executed at, and the cited executing witness are execution evidence, not design criteria: they live in ONE typed receipt, gunbc.native_witness_transition_receipt native_at_small_scale_transition_receipt, and are restated neither here nor in gunbc.design_document (operator ruling on gunbc#7710, 2026-08-02 — this note and the design document previously carried independent hand-maintained copies of the same advancing status). Staged expectations (not flat 30–35min): Stage A modest admission saving only; Stage B first order-of-magnitude witness reduction after production native cutover; Stage C five-minute gate when all conjunction in docs/plans/five-minute-ci-gate-design.md holds. Dispositions: entry-graph-union CLOSED; retention PARKED (#7581). See docs/plans/five-minute-ci-gate-design.md."

data native_selected_witness_bundle_frontier_note: String = "THE MEASURED FRONTIER BEHIND native-selected-witness-bundle, moved off the ticket brief when it exceeded the 100-word page budget. The 2026-08-10 recut authored it at 177 words and nothing refused it, because the budget witness had never executed: it merged in #8111 on a CANCELLED check. Nothing is dropped here — the full authored text follows, and the brief now cites this symbol rather than restating it. STOPPED AND RE-CUT (operator ruling 2026-08-10, superseding the 2026-08-08 one-PR mandate this row used to carry). #8043/#8080 attempted the complete cutover in one PR and is closed as quarry; the row survives because the CAPABILITY is real and the SCOPE was wrong. Root, in the operator's words: v2 native execution entails a real self-host frontier and must be named as such — not carried as a CI-performance step. The frontier is measured, not estimated: of 11 rejecting members in one real 15-file std closure, 5 are normalize CONTRACT VIOLATIONS (it retains wrapper declarations under its declared lowered | wrapper-retained\{cause\} 'corpus stays green' frontier, then its own module-grain well_formed gate rejects the tree those retentions live in), 2 are the graft dissolution guard working correctly, 3 are genuine frontend gaps (dag/std/types at LEX; src/v2/std/node and dag/std/content_hash at PARSE, the where-refinement form), and 1 went uncaptured. A broken contract is a bounded repair with a known intended behaviour; a missing capability is a program — so the 5 and the 3 are different work and do not schedule together."

data native_selected_witness_bundle_exact_head_recut_note: String = "THE 2026-08-11 EXACT-HEAD RE-CUT of native-selected-witness-bundle, moved off the ticket brief to stay inside the 100-word page budget the brief is measured against. FIRST SLICE: RE-CUT AGAIN BY EXACT-HEAD RE-OBSERVATION (2026-08-11, main c03be069687): the 'five bounded normalize repairs, then three syntax gaps' sequence this row carried is RETIRED, because it no longer describes the tree — see docs/plans/v2-frontend-std-ingestion-frontier-exact-head.md, which re-observes the same 15-member subject and preserves the e588031201 receipt unchanged as history. Two premises failed by execution: dag/std/algebra.dag is a LEX member, not a normalize contract violation (so the retention population is 4, not 5), and the ENTRY module now rejects at PARSE where the historical receipt had it accepting. Neither half is a bounded repair any more. The normalize half is NOT a well_formed exemption — the original body-lowering contract (#6520) deliberately made local lowering total while keeping recursive well_formed as the SOLE structural wall, so scoping that wall around surface wrappers would reverse the safety decision rather than repair it. The real defect is that the typed frontier is only a diagnostic convention: body_lower_finish_for_normalize converts EVERY Rejected into retention while discarding its diagnostics, BodyLoweringFrontierDisposition has no rejected arm so a genuine rejection classifies as Lowered, retention is recognised from the diagnostic HEAD which rejected_with_pending systematically makes wrong, NormalizedTree is a bare alias to Node, and resolve consumes that alias — so nothing structurally stops a retained mixed tree reaching resolve. THREE INHERITED ATTRIBUTIONS WERE REFUTED BY EXECUTION (2026-08-11), and two of them had repairs already proposed against them: the types.dag fixed-width \\xNN escape hypothesis is FALSE (the escape lexes; the member still refuses after the annotation channel landed, so its wall is a third unattributed cause), the node.dag qualified-record-constructor hypothesis is FALSE (a.b.C \{ id: 1 \} parses and reaches Accepted), and the em-dash attribution authored in this lane was FALSE one layer down. Only content_hash's where-refinement form is confirmed (PARSE refusal against a passing plain-alias control). Every attribution in this frontier that was not executed has so far been wrong, so no member repair may be scheduled from a remaining description. The syntax half is likewise a capability, not three patches: dag/std/algebra.dag's lex wall is the UNWIRED §4c annotation channel — dag_lex_rules registers no AnnotationRule for '//', so a comment tokenises as two slash tokens plus whatever its payload happens to lex as, and it fails at the first character with no semantic rule (em-dash, backtick, '@' all refuse; '-' passes). ASCII comment specimens are therefore FALSE CONTROLS, and adding an em-dash case would entrench the missing channel. Sequence: honest body-lowering frontier -> resolve-ready normalized-tree construction boundary -> current retained-body population reaches zero -> frontend syntax population. DEFERRED WITH ITS SHAS, not lost: the sugar capture-slot repair chain 6888b976e6 -> f62e8388a7 -> c84842c98e lands together or not at all — cherry-picked clean onto main it is 5/5 FAIL, because it reads a three-part capture slot needing a grammar production main lacks. Separability was asserted from a description and refuted by execution; nothing in this row is scheduled on a description again.\n\nHANDBACK: SUPERSEDED BY EXACT-HEAD RE-OBSERVATION (2026-08-11): this field previously promised the next reader a THREE-ITEM PROGRAM, which the same re-cut retired in first_slice — the row was simultaneously retiring and promising one program. The handback is now the four-stage sequence: honest body-lowering frontier, then the resolve-ready normalized-tree construction boundary, then the retained population reaching zero, then the frontend syntax population. Four states are reported separately and never merged. COMPLETED REPAIR: genuine body-lowering rejections propagate instead of being relabelled as retention (retention keeps exactly one producer, the explicit unregistered-identity arm), and the production '//' annotation channel is registered on dag_lex_rules, both with discriminating controls executed at construction and LexArtifact grain. THREE TIME GRAINS, never merged into one population. (1) PRE-REPAIR PARTIAL OBSERVATION at c03be069687: 10 of 15 members measured, four normalize retention members (logic, optional, diagnostic, occurrence_identity), two lex walls (types, dag/std/algebra), the entry at parse, three accepted; node.dag a budget interruption and four members never run. (2) POST-REPAIR EXECUTED, and only these: logic.dag NORM_RETAINED -> NORM_OTHER, optional.dag and diagnostic.dag still NORM_RETAINED. logic.dag leaving retention is the repair working rather than the member closing — it still does not ingest; its refusal is merely reported as the refusal it always was. (3) POST-REPAIR UNKNOWN, and this set may carry no scheduling conclusion: occurrence_identity (retained pre-repair, NOT rerun), the entry, types, node, content_hash, both graft rows, and both algebra rows — dag/std/algebra in particular was not re-observed after the lexer repair, so the lex wall is claimed closed on minimal pairs and not on that member. The current retained population is therefore NOT the pre-repair four; it is two confirmed plus one unrerun. UNMEASURED: node.dag and dag/std/algebra.dag are budget interruptions, not verdicts, and src/v2/std/algebra.dag was never captured in either receipt — none of the three may carry a scheduling conclusion, and completing the 15-member batch needs an instrument that does not exceed budget on the larger members. STILL OWED AS CONSTRUCTION: NormalizedTree is a bare alias to Node and resolve consumes it, so a retained tree is kept out of resolve by propagation rather than by construction. Native witness execution is complete only when it stops being a self-host question, and that is measured by the frontier reaching zero, never by a wall-clock reading."

data v2_lens_suite_execution_block_note: String = "THE RESIDUE AND PER-LENS EXECUTION CONTRACT BEHIND v2-lens-suite-execution, moved off the ticket brief when it exceeded the 100-word page budget (authored at 203 words in the same 2026-08-10 recut, under the same unexecuted budget witness). Nothing is dropped here — the full authored text follows. BLOCKED, AND THE BLOCK IS HONEST (2026-08-10): the former trigger — CI2-0 terminal acceptance — is unreachable, because that lane is stopped and its one-PR shape retired. This row keeps its dependency on the native row deliberately rather than being re-anchored around it: its own handback demands ZERO v1 lens-body executions, which is native execution by definition, so relaxing the trigger would only move the frontier into the handback. Its residue lives in #8077, an ownerless draft whose concurrency portion already merged separately as #8112; the genuine remainder is the six-module lens suite. The underlying concern is DESIGN section 6's, and it does not expire with the lane: an executable hygiene check must keep every lens either wired or deleted, because an inert lens is coverage by illusion. Roster derived from the existing v2 lens registry — no second hand-maintained suite list; every registry identity appears exactly once in the plan; every applicable lens body executes through the v2/CI2 route with ordinary v1 interpreter lens executions zero. Each lens returns a reading or a typed located refusal — Unavailable retains its exact trigger and counts as executed, never as accepted capability. One exact whole-corpus fact pack per process; a repeated query constructs nothing."

data namespace_node_recut_note: String = "THE BROAD NAMESPACE NODE WAS TOO COARSE TO CLOSE HONESTLY, and the recut is the fix (operator ruling, 2026-07-31). namespace-canonical-binding previously combined two separable things in one boundary: working out which declarations a name can see, and calling one decision function on them. A check proving only the none/one/many decision could therefore have marked the whole node accepted while candidate derivation, reference-derived dependency closure, and the production changeover all remained unbuilt — an acceptance hazard, and the exact shape of rung inflation DESIGN 4b forbids, where a carrier named for the top rung occupies the bottom one.\\n\\nThree prerequisites now stand in front of it. namespace-binding-kernel owns the decision alone, on a candidate population SUPPLIED to it. namespace-reference-derived-closure owns structural exposure, authored order, the candidate index, exact reference-to-declaration binding, and the derived dependency edges. namespace-ambiguity-discharge settles the genuinely-many cases from real compilation. namespace-canonical-binding KEEPS ITS DURABLE IDENTITY and is now the final production changeover only, so historical links resolve and no identity is reused.\\n\\nWhy the split falls exactly there: dependency edges are a PROJECTION OF THE BINDING, not a second authored statement. A program that instead authored the missing edges by hand reached 400 of 771 files at roughly one import per CI floor before it was stopped; the unresolved population was evidence that binding and module discovery are coupled at the wrong boundary, not a backlog to grind down.\\n\\nTHE CHANGEOVER AND ITS SUCCESSOR ARE DISJOINT, and an earlier revision of this recut broke that (review 45649). It retitled namespace-canonical-binding as 'switch the whole compiler over' with a boundary reading 'every place that resolves a name', which swallowed namespace-bound-only-consumers underneath it — that node's own boundary is type checking, call lookup, and argument-count checks reading the decided answer. Overlapping boundaries are the §2 redundancy this document exists to remove, and they are worse on a roadmap than in code: completing the parent would already entail most of the child, so either the child can never be honestly accepted or the parent was silently read narrower than it was written. The cut is PRODUCER versus READER. The changeover node owns the sites that WORK OUT what a name refers to, and the deletion of the search-everything fallback behind them. Its successor owns the READERS of that answer and their obligation to stop on unresolved or ambiguous. Neither entails the other, and each can be accepted on its own evidence.\\n\\nONE EDGE WAS DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED. pderive-source-slot-binding still depends on namespace-canonical-binding, which now means it waits for the whole production changeover. It plausibly needs only occurrence transport plus the binding kernel, but that is unproven: the dependency moves only once the focused P-derive consumer demonstrates it can operate on an exact supplied candidate population. Loosening it on the strength of the argument alone would be asserting a fact nobody has measured."

data compute_consumer_admission_sequencing_note: String = "THE RULE THAT ORDERS THE COMPUTE LANE, and it is a sequencing ruling rather than a design preference (operator, 2026-08-07): do not move the present arrangement onto our own machines. Move exact computations onto one shared fabric, and DELETE THE DUPLICATED WORK BEFORE increasing the number of things asking for it. Handing agents a build capability without deduplication and admission would not be a fabric — it would be a tidier way for ten callers to launch ten cold builds of one tree, which is the failure the lane exists to prevent. That is why compute-deduplication-and-admission stands in front of ci-owned-execution in the graph rather than beside it: owning CI adds a consumer, and a consumer added before the duplication is removed multiplies the load instead of sharing it.\n\nTHE SECOND HALF OF THE SAME RULE APPLIES TO NATIVE EXECUTION. Emitting a native witness bundle and running it is the right destination, and the miniature is decisive at the scale it measures — direct native calls in single-digit milliseconds against tens interpreted and hundreds through warm cargo transport. But the cited production enrolment delivered zero of three native and three of three fallback, so the required path took no benefit from it, and native bodies surrounded by duplicated preparation would still be bad CI. Native realization and shared preparation are ONE programme, not two lanes competing for the same slot; native-selected-witness-bundle owns the first, and the discovery snapshot, scoped substrate, early selection and streaming rows own the second.\n\nWHY THE MECHANISM ROWS ARE A CHAIN AND NOT A SET. The measured floor is dominated by preparation rather than by the work being prepared for: on the clearest full-floor subject, the discovery batch spent the large majority of its wall on setup and resolve and a small minority actually evaluating witnesses, and the two workers walked the same roots twice. Each row therefore removes a DIFFERENT duplicate — the second walk, the second initialised world, preparation that precedes selection, and the barrier between preparing and executing — and each is only measurable once the one before it has landed. Chaining them with dependency edges is what keeps at most the next one startable, so the standing limit on concurrent performance mechanisms falls out of the graph rather than being restated as prose that nothing enforces. Width two is deliberately absent from that chain and stays parked: the tested implementation shared typed bytes while each worker still built its own world, and the architectural prerequisite is that no second private semantic world exists."

data product_interface_convergence_note: String = "THE PERMANENT PRODUCT INTERFACE IS TWO OPERATIONS (operator convergence mandate 2026-08-09): gunbc build <program> and gunbc test <program>. DEVBOOT, CI2, CONFIDENCE, CONVERGE, materialization and lenses are implementation responsibilities behind those operations, never separate user workflows — the caller never chooses runner, cache, affected-set algorithm, interpreter, bundle partition, realization provider, lease, ref, store, or host. #8049 owns gunbc build (the caller sees Built with program subject, artifact and receipt, or a typed refusal — never leases or refs); #8043 owns the reusable v2 test-plan execution behind gunbc test; V2-LENS-0 and dirty-worktree verification consume both. An incomplete affected-set answer selects the COMPLETE v2 test plan — never zero tests, never the interpreter. CI converges toward gunbc test with an exact tested-merge-tree subject: local-versus-CI becomes subject and policy, not separate architecture. Cross-process edge-index materialization is SUPPORTING WORK inside LENS-0/DEVBOOT, not a sixth program; before it builds, the remaining gates hold: attribute the un-decomposed resolve residue to its own seam, reproduce the cold misses in a fresh process, compare miss keys across at least two corpus subjects, prove no other in-process consumer reconstructs the value — then add a request family to the EXISTING materialization provider, never a parallel cache, and only after content-derived SourceFile identity lands (a deserialized index and a freshly built one must agree by construction). Artifact reuse identity stays pure and process-independent (content, environment, phase, policy, algorithm); producer and consumer process coordinates — invocation, host identity, boot identity, pid, process start identity, executable digest — live in production and consumption receipts and leases, extending DEVBOOT's existing lease and attempt vocabulary, never the artifact key."

data roadmap_execution_contract_frontier_note: String = "Every node below is ExecutionContractUnspecified: the declared, fail-closed migration frontier for gunbc.roadmap_execution_contract. A node states the exact validation operations that close it before the actuator will spawn for it, so dispatch refuses with a typed environment-admission diagnostic rather than guessing validations or dependencies. The prior binding lived on a pre-refresh operator-TODO node deleted by the 2026-07-27 authority refresh; re-binding is per-node roadmap authoring, never a merge-time default."

fn authored(identity: String,
  id: String, done: Bool, content: String) -> RoadmapNode {
  RoadmapNode {
    identity: identity as RoadmapNodeIdentity,
    node: nid(s: id),
    line: AuthoredLine { done: done, content: content },
    carriers: [],
    sizing: Unsized,
    execution: ExecutionContractUnspecified,
    owner: "",
    signoff: Unsigned,
  }
}

