  )
}

data v1_interpreter_primitive_roster_execution_contract_note: String = "THE CLOSING CHECK IS STRUCTURAL, NOT A POPULATION PIN, and that choice is the whole content of this binding. The node asks whether the interpreter's dispatch surface is ENUMERABLE and whether its roster can silently disagree with the dispatch; it does not ask how large the surface currently is. So the bound validation asserts properties that survive the roster legitimately growing -- named dispatch sites contribute derived rows, duplicate row keys refuse, shadows are exactly the known set BY NAME, every declared row carries its own dissolution trigger, an arm carrying no semantic primitive identity stays representable, and an unrecognised form label refuses rather than defaulting.\n\nBinding it to counts would have re-created at the acceptance layer the exact defect #7615 removed from the witness layer: the five deleted witnesses pinned live-population numbers copied from the tree, which DESIGN.md 5 rules is not an oracle, and they duly behaved as pure change detectors that redded main twice. A closing check that reds on legitimate growth is worse than one that does not exist, because it trains everyone to edit the number rather than read the change.\n\nThe validation can genuinely fail: removing a dispatch site, dropping a declared row's trigger, admitting an unknown form label, or letting a second arm identity shadow a spelling each red it. The detectors' own discriminating REDs and positive controls live in test.claim.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface_witness_test and execute beside it."

fn v1_interpreter_primitive_roster_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
    entry: "dag/test/claim/v1_interpreter_primitive_roster_acceptance_test.dag" as FilePath,
    function: "v1_interpreter_primitive_roster_acceptance_contract_holds" as NonEmptyStr,
  )
}

data v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_execution_contract_note: String = "THE CLOSING CHECK FOR v1-interpreter-primitive-dispatch-authority. R1 inverts the roster: gunbc.v1_interpreter_primitive_surface v1_interpreter_authored_roster_arms is the canonical authority as authored InterpreterPrimitiveDispatchArm rows; v1_interpreter_dispatch_emit derives Rust enum variant names from arm identity and generates lookup tables. Compile-time exhaustiveness is site-scoped: single-family dispatch sites get a non-wildcard enum match; eval_call_bridge and eval_call_native_intercept share one enum per site but expand per-family subsets with a required wildcard (missing handler body is runtime unreachable!, not compile error — per-family enum split is follow-up). Structural properties that survive roster growth are asserted here; R0 discriminating controls remain in v1_interpreter_primitive_surface_witness_test."

fn v1_interpreter_primitive_dispatch_authority_execution_contract() -> WorkItemExecutionContract {
  gunbc_claim_execution_contract(
