    active_large(
      identity: "rn_8QK2M5F7V3N9P1R4T6W0X2Y5Z8A",
      id: "five-minute-ci-gate",
      owner: "ci-cost",
      path: "docs/plans/five-minute-ci-gate-design.md",
      t: fields(
        headline: "Serve every required CI operation with the bare minimum computation; five minutes is the distress ceiling, not the contract",
        boundary: "Every required operation performs only the computation its inputs require — no semantic fact recomputed whose inputs did not change (re-anchored by operator ruling 2026-08-02: five minutes is the distress ceiling — the Stage C checkpoint bound, not the contract). Sub-lanes (unordered roster — dispatch order follows the graph edges): #7522 warm-merge-admission net receipt; #7534 materialization substrate; union closed → per-entry assembly; the mechanism chain (discovery snapshot, scoped substrate, early selection, streaming); this registration. THE NATIVE ROW NO LONGER PRECEDES THIS GATE (2026-08-10): that edge is deleted, so this gate is schedulable without waiting on a self-host frontier.",
        displaced_cost: "MEASURED DECOMPOSITION, which relocates the whole lane: a 3,290s floor is 1,422s discovery/setup, 690s scoped worker, and 97s of actual witness evaluation. CI is not running tests — it is repeatedly reconstructing an understanding of the repository so that millisecond tests can run. Three consequences follow and each is a row rather than an opinion: ordinary and scoped discovery duplicate the same walk at 295.7s + 284.3s; selection is sharp about meaning and blunt about cost, deciding what matters only AFTER roster, index and closure are already paid for; and cache hits are effectively all-or-nothing, one missing typed key costing 82-96 percent of a full cold symbol-index build. The unit being reused is too small — values are cached while the world that gives them meaning is rebuilt.",
        first_slice: "Register sequence and staged expectations in authority; land no implementation under the parent id — the native cutover's whole implementation belongs to the CI-0 child row.",
        red_control: "A sub-lane that widens to whole-corpus work, silently falls through from an incomplete materialization artifact to cold recompute, or claims the five-minute envelope without Stage C fleet receipts refuses rather than greens.",
        out_of_scope: "No single PR closes the parent; placement/build-flake cap-first work, tokenizer escape scan, and closed entry-graph-union stay outside.",
        handback: "Sequence graph, staged expectations, six sub-lane rows, and design note in docs/plans/five-minute-ci-gate-design.md."
      )
    ),
    active(
      identity: "rn_1H4J6L8N0P2Q5S7U9V1W3X6Y8Z0B",
      id: "warm-merge-admission",
      owner: "ci-cost",
      path: "docs/plans/five-minute-ci-gate-design.md",
      t: fields(
        headline: "Admit merges from warm stamped receipts, not cold recomputation",
        boundary: "#7522 in flight (dispatch order follows the graph edges): fold resolve and materialization receipt gates into merge admission so the pull-request path stamps once and admits from warm receipts. Operator expectation: probable net recovery ~1–1.5 min (not ~3 min) — final-head run decides; not transcribed as receipt until measured.",
        displaced_cost: "Merge admission and the floor tail currently pay separate cold paths for facts already fixed when the run started.",
        first_slice: "Finish #7522 with real net wall receipt and stage profile.",
        red_control: "A stale base-tree or stale gate-roster receipt blocks merge; a missing or invalid receipt refuses rather than widening to a full rerun.",
        out_of_scope: "No change to main-push cold controls or the falsifier cadence.",
        handback: "One admission path with discriminating stale-base, stale-roster, and fresh controls executed."
      )
    ),
    active_large(
      identity: "rn_2I5K7M9O1Q3R6T8V0W2X4Y7Z9A1C",
      id: "native-selected-witness-bundle",
      owner: "ci-cost",
      path: "docs/plans/five-minute-ci-gate-design.md",
      t: fields(
        headline: "Name the v2 self-host frontier that native witness execution actually requires, and close it stage by stage",
        boundary: "STOPPED AND RE-CUT (operator ruling 2026-08-10, superseding the 2026-08-08 one-PR mandate this row carried). #8043/#8080 attempted the complete cutover in one PR and is closed as quarry; the row survives because the CAPABILITY is real and the SCOPE was wrong. Root, in the operator's words: v2 native execution entails a real self-host frontier and must be named as such, not carried as a CI-performance step. The frontier is gunbc.roadmap_authority native_selected_witness_bundle_frontier_note (historical) and native_selected_witness_bundle_exact_head_recut_note (current).",
        displaced_cost: "The stopped lane still paid for itself twice. It produced two merged frontend repairs (#8114: arrow-lambda grammar admission, and the graft dissolution guard — main accepted hollow-shell modules until it landed, proven by reverting only namespace_graft.dag and watching both RED witnesses fail), and it produced the frontier table that replaced an eleven-item guess with a three-item program — a table since superseded by the 2026-08-11 exact-head re-observation, under which the split is four normalize members and two independent lex walls, not five and three. What it disproved is equally load-bearing: this row no longer parents five-minute-ci-gate, because witness EVALUATION is 97s of a 3,290s floor — an infinitely fast evaluator leaves 97 percent of the floor standing, so native execution was never the CI-cost lever and CI cost must not wait on a self-host frontier.",
        first_slice: "Superseded by exact-head re-observation (2026-08-11): neither half is a bounded repair. Sequence, and the full re-cut with its three time grains, is gunbc.roadmap_authority native_selected_witness_bundle_exact_head_recut_note — honest body-lowering frontier, then the resolve-ready normalized-tree construction boundary, then the retained population reaching zero, then the frontend syntax population.",
        red_control: "A member reported as a frontend GAP whose refusal is actually normalize's own retention contradicting itself refuses the classification — the two populations are separated by reading the rejection reason as a containment read, never by the first reason rendered, because rejected_with_pending prepends accepted-carrier diagnostics to a later rejection and the FIRST reason is systematically wrong. A cohort claimed as reaching Accepted whose closure contains no Accepted member refuses. A repair asserted separable from a description, without a cherry-pick onto main executed green, refuses.",
        out_of_scope: "No CI wall-clock claim of any kind is made or scheduled here — that dependency is deleted (see displaced_cost). No second body-lowering, resolution, or classification authority beside the existing ones. No Interpreted execution route — InterpreterSubjectTest describes the subject under test and never grants v1 the scheduler. Not the complete-cutover-in-one-PR shape: it was attempted, and the cohort was empty at the real frontier.",
        handback: "Reported by time grain, never as one population: pre-repair partial observation, post-repair executed, post-repair unknown. The three grains and what each contains are gunbc.roadmap_authority native_selected_witness_bundle_exact_head_recut_note. Native witness execution is complete only when it stops being a self-host question, measured by the frontier reaching zero, never by a wall-clock reading."
      )
    ),
    active_large(
      identity: "rn_7Q2W4E6R8T1Y3V5P9A2S4D6F8G1H",
      id: "v2-lens-suite-execution",
