      path: "docs/plans/five-minute-ci-gate-design.md",
      t: fields(
        headline: "V2-LENS-0: every registered v2 lens executes over one exact corpus subject through the CI2 route",
        boundary: "BLOCKED, AND THE BLOCK IS HONEST (2026-08-10): the former trigger, CI2-0 terminal acceptance, is unreachable because that lane is stopped and its one-PR shape retired. This row keeps its dependency on the native row deliberately rather than being re-anchored around it: its own handback demands ZERO v1 lens-body executions, which is native execution by definition, so relaxing the trigger would only move the frontier into the handback. The underlying concern is DESIGN section 6's and does not expire with the lane: an inert lens is coverage by illusion. Residue, roster derivation and the per-lens execution contract are gunbc.roadmap_authority v2_lens_suite_execution_block_note.",
        displaced_cost: "Registry completeness proves metadata coherence, not execution: many LensContract rows carry NoConsumerWitness, and an inert lens is coverage by illusion. Binary acquisition, not lens logic, was the recurring execution failure; #8054 proved a whole-corpus query executes and its expense is corpus-fact construction, not lens evaluation.",
        first_slice: "Dispatch trigger (operator 2026-08-09): one ordinary NON-FIXTURE test declaration completes canonical parse-normalize-resolve-infer-realize-execute in #8043, with the removed parser diagnostic named, a planted nearby syntax RED still refusing, and the roster identity joined. Checkpoint A: one deliberately boring lens selected MECHANICALLY from the registry (deterministic, hermetic, no host effect, no base-revision graph, small fact input) — a checkpoint, never a completed capsule. Checkpoint B: derive the complete roster, execute all through one shared fact pack, one LensSuiteReceipt. Checkpoint C: enroll the suite permanently in gunbc test.",
        red_control: "Permanence laws: registering a lens AUTO-ENROLLS it (a registry row without an executable body reds gunbc test; a deleted lens leaving a row reds the roster join); executing zero lenses can never produce a successful suite verdict; registered = planned = terminal outcomes with zero duplicates and zero unaccounted; ordinary v1 lens-body executions and fallback are zero. A missing input yields Partial, Unavailable, or Refused — never an empty success. Fact-pack construction is once per process, a second query constructs zero, warm execution within five seconds. The delivery/consumption question returns as ONE lens here (advisory until declaration grain), never a standalone workflow.",
        out_of_scope: "No new universal lens ontology, no separate lens scheduler, no report-only successor PRs. Host or v1-produced input facts may remain explicit temporary bridges but may not decide a lens answer.",
        handback: "One LensSuiteReceipt on one exact corpus subject with zero v1 lens-body executions and at least one real downstream consumer — initially gunbc test — reading it."
      )
    ),
