        headline: "One ledger for what the CI-speed work actually bought",
        boundary: "One row per attempt made across this arc: what it predicted, what it changed, the exact subject it was measured on, the movement inside its own segment, the movement in the whole required path, whether memory stayed inside the fixed envelope, and a typed result — delivered, partial, falsified, confounded by infrastructure, or evidence invalid — with what each one implies next. Rows are read out of receipts that already exist; nothing is re-measured to fill this in.",
        displaced_cost: "Weeks of work bought real causal knowledge and several correctly killed hypotheses, but the required path is not meaningfully shorter. Without this ledger the next programme re-runs the attempts already falsified, and re-argues the ones that were only confounded by a machine failure.",
        first_slice: "Fill the ledger from the receipts already landed, and state the whole-path movement the arc actually achieved.",
        red_control: "An attempt whose claimed movement cannot be tied to an executed receipt is recorded as evidence invalid, never as delivered. A win inside one segment with no movement in the whole path is partial, never delivered. A result from a run the machine killed is confounded, not falsified — collapsing those two loses the distinction the ledger exists to make.",
        out_of_scope: "No new measurement programme and no new optimisation. This row explains the arc; it does not extend it.",
        handback: "The ledger with every attempt classified, and the next mechanisms it justifies, each named with the cost it is expected to remove."
      )
    ),
