        displaced_cost: "Across six entries sharing one index, typecheck_compute grew 2.86x while the fixed loading row grew only 1.08x; selected closures repeat membership 35.9–38.4x by module count and 43.0–49.3x by bytes. Slice 2 converted that membership duplication into a decision ratio and found zero repeated typecheck compute at every measured cell — the priced benefit of union construction is absent at N≤50.",
        first_slice: "Delivered: slice-2 attribution matrix, controls in docs/plans/entry-graph-union-slice2-typecheck-attribution.md §C–F, operator no-go verdict §F.",
        red_control: "Satisfied by execution: attribution reconciles on exclusive (entry,module_key) basis without inferring computation from closure membership; reorder preserves the distinct-compute set; decision_ratio=0 at every measured N≤50 cell. The durable post-instrument witness is shared_typecheck_distinct_compute_count_is_order_invariant.",
        out_of_scope: "No union graph implementation, no eviction redesign, and no forking of the entry-closure memo already in flight — sharing more while holding more live collides with retention.",
        handback: "docs/plans/entry-graph-union-slice2-typecheck-attribution.md §F verdict plus committed measurement receipts under docs/plans/receipts/entry-graph-union-slice2/; no implementation proposal (no-go)."
