      path: "docs/plans/fleet-self-converge-enforcement-design.md",
      t: fields(
        headline: "Count every automatic job-runner recovery, and say what retires it",
        boundary: "The timer that restarts wedged job runners records each firing — which machine, which slot, what it observed, what it did, and whether it worked — and those counts reach the fleet's health. Deciding locally that a runner has stopped making progress is kept separate from asking the provider whether it is still registered, so recovery keeps working during the outage it exists for.",
