        first_slice: "Emit one attributable receipt per firing, and show the rate per machine.",
        red_control: "A restart with no attributable cause is not recorded as a recovery. Failing to reach the provider refuses rather than being read as offline. Nothing restarts a slot that is currently running work.",
        out_of_scope: "Not replacing the current two-part test with a bare silence rule before the local part has been proven on its own.",
        handback: "The counted receipts, the split by cause, and the named condition under which this timer is deleted."
      )
    ),
    active(
      identity: "rn_HYV4E84MRC1MJ73EDJZYXP89S8",
      id: "fleet-spark-host-enrollment",
      owner: "fleet",
      path: "dag/gunbc/dgx_spark_procurement.dag",
      t: fields(
        headline: "Turn the two Spark machines from hand-managed boxes into exact fleet members",
        boundary: "srv5 and srv6 become fleet members: enrollment intents carrying InferenceServingParticipation, with endpoint rows derived downstream from the assigned reservation rows — re-typing the address literal refuses, a reverse import into the network intent refuses, and the join is a projection between the two existing authorities, never a second host-identity authority. Enrollment constructs their four required lifecycle cells — identity converge, reach, compute-fabric enrolment, assimilation complete — and every cell stays honestly Unobserved until an observation producer answers it. Enrolled is not converged: no identity convergence, reach satisfaction, capacity acceptance, or serving claim lives here.",
