        displaced_cost: "Whether a concept already exists, who consumes it, what executes it, and what a deletion would break are today answered by grep, memory, or not at all — every session re-derives them, duplicates get minted beside existing authorities, and the reverse question is simulated with N forward closures. This deterministic layer is also the grounding packet the judgment service requires: without it, the machine judgement lane has nothing checkable to stand on. Acceptance standing (2026-08-08, post-rework): the reverse query is merged; the changed-surface rework closed departed-path consumption, the typed Complete/Partial/Refused outcome (unresolved input contaminates the whole result), the skip-authority wall (SkipAuthorityGranted reachable only from Complete AND exact), optional cycle analysis, the two-direction selector-parity control, and three real-diff receipts — one of which falsified a fixture assumption (git reports a deletion in both projections). OPEN: the base-graph population — a deleted subject resolves to typed BaseGraphUnavailable because every graph reader is head-only; building revision-scoped reading is an operator decision (new seed Rust or a heavy checkout). Measured correction: cycles were 28 percent of the wall, not most — the dominant cost is resolve and fact production.",
        first_slice: "One real corpus query usable by a person — a real module, its explained dependent tree at the finest honestly available grain, with the completeness standing shown — through a tools entry, not a new CLI arm. Not just a fixture suite: the fixture-only consumer is the pattern this lane exists to stop.",
        red_control: "A query whose subject module does not exist refuses rather than answering empty. A planted unbound module appears in the standing, and no reading over a pool with unaccounted members reports itself closed. The result may not claim one-sided incompleteness while pool independence is unavailable — the standing carries the trigger. A second edge producer beside the declared single authority refuses. Forward-intent refusals (operator amendment 2026-08-08): a branch name without an exact revision is not a subject; a deleted declaration is never silently resolved against the head tree; an unresolved input never becomes an empty result; a partial universe cannot report that no relevant authority exists — no-matches and could-not-see-enough remain different answers. The deterministic layer never turns prose into repository identity: it returns the bounded universe, exact candidate declarations, consumers, explanation paths, and standing for a later mapper or judge.",
        out_of_scope: "No LLM, no Spark, no provider — this is deterministic repository inspection and must work with none of them provisioned. Declaration and node grain arrive through the namespace dependency-projection triggers, never through a parallel host bridge.",
        handback: "The reading with typed direction and standing, adapters above it, one real corpus query a person can run and read, and the judgment lane re-grounded on the packet this produces."
      )
