        displaced_cost: "The grouping move — five things consumed the same way become one new layer — is how this repository forms layers at all, and today it happens only when a person notices: duplicates get minted beside existing authorities, boutique implementations accumulate until a consolidation pays the fork back at interest, and the judgment of which lens a similarity holds under is re-derived by hand every time. The candidate that is NOT an abstraction is half the value: the Spark endpoint question burned a session on topology surgery that a projection-missing classification — join the existing authorities downstream, mint nothing — would have answered in one line.",
