        displaced_cost: "Without it the probe child mints throwaway identifiers that immediately require migration, and two carriers of the same fact drift.",
        first_slice: "The identity and receipt types, with a synthetic-receipt round-trip witness.",
        red_control: "A duplicate class id reds the registry witness (executed). Receipt identity fields are required-by-shape with no Optional arms — corpus-wide construction ENFORCEMENT of that shape is deliberately not this node's claim: it is the floor-record-construction-wall class's bar, the same split the module's receipt_identity_note states (honesty reconciliation, review 46861 — the original bar claimed an unwritability wall Stage 0 never owned).",
        out_of_scope: "No probes, no dispositions, no rung derivation, no prevalence.",
        handback: "The schema module path and the identity-registry witness receipt."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_T6JTXDKQBI6FDZ742FSGRZRQNA", id: "ladder-probe-corpus",
