      t: fields(
        headline: "Unknown labels and surplus positionals refuse at the direct-call seam — LANDED (gunbc#7519, merged 2026-07-31)",
        boundary: "ACCEPTED fragment, recut from floor-call-shape-wall at its actual grain (operator spine verdict). CallArgumentNameUnknown + CallPositionalSurplus blocking, exemption-free, mirroring call_function_inner's two refused classes (underscore idiom included); census refused 28 live parameter-rename fossils, all fixed; the silent emit-path reorder retired for Accepted programs. What did NOT land stays on the sibling nodes: missing/duplicate, signature-resolution coverage, the method seam.",
        displaced_cost: "The mislabeled call that computed the wrong thing silently on the emission path is unwritable in an Accepted program at this seam.",
        first_slice: "DONE — acceptance receipt: merged gunbc#7519; pre/post probe pair; suite green; regen divergence 0.",
        red_control: "ct_call_shape_wall_witness_test — migrates to the probe corpus as this class's durable pair.",
        out_of_scope: "Everything the sibling nodes own.",
        handback: "Receipt recorded; residue on call-missing-and-duplicate-wall and call-signature-resolution-coverage."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_EXUHLON5V24YU7Z4XLJFWEZO33", id: "call-missing-and-duplicate-wall",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeSmall,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Duplicate-argument half LANDED (gunbc#7847); missing-argument half remains",
        boundary: "CORRECTED FRAMING (parent review, 2026-08-05): the defect is two ACTUALS resolving to the SAME PARAMETER, not 'duplicate labels' — positional-then-named onto one slot, or two labels both satisfying an underscore-shorthand parameter. Keyed by resolved binding target: a NAMED actual keys on its own label; a POSITIONAL actual keys on the parameter its index fills, matching call_function_inner. call_function_inner refuses (CallArgumentDuplicate) before the compile-seam mirror, keeping both authorities in agreement. Fixed a prior compile-seam bug where declared-parameter matching let underscore-shorthand steal a later exact-named match (false positive in cardinality.dag). Missing required arguments remain unrefused; param_node_default_value legitimately fills omissions and must stay green.",
        displaced_cost: "Two actuals resolving to one parameter previously let the last-bound value win silently, unlocatable at the call site; a missing argument surfacing as NoSuchVariable inside the body blames the wrong site.",
        first_slice: "DONE — the duplicate half: interpreter refusal in call_function_inner, compile-seam mirror keyed on resolved binding target (not label-string equality), guarantee-probe corpus rows and dark-suite witness migrated, disposition-count witnesses updated. Remaining: the missing-argument half, default-value-aware, probe-paired the same way.",
        red_control: "Landed: mixed positional+named duplicate (one(1, a: 2)) refuses on both authorities; every corpus form incl. underscore-shorthand params stays green. Remaining: missing non-default arg refuses on both authorities; defaulted omissions stay green.",
        out_of_scope: "Label membership (landed sibling); the method seam.",
        handback: "Duplicate half: both authorities' refusal sites, census delta, probe receipts — delivered in gunbc#7847. Missing half: still owed."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_GVLXWYYRQV47WTJLSSIFX7FLFM", id: "call-signature-resolution-coverage",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeSmall,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Signature-resolution coverage: the sig-unresolved fallthrough stops being a blind spot",
        boundary: "A call whose callee resolves NO signature bypasses every call-shape judgment (measured: 3 label fossils invisible to the landed wall in dag_collect, found only by grep). Either the callee resolves and is judged, or the failure to resolve is itself a typed, counted fact — never a silent fallthrough to the method bridge. Rides the namespace lane's resolution coverage; this node owns the call-shape consequence.",
        displaced_cost: "The wall's own measured blind spot: correctness there currently rests on grep.",
        first_slice: "Count the fallthrough (typed, per-module) so the blind spot has a size before it has a fix.",
        red_control: "The dag_collect specimen class reds if reintroduced once coverage lands; fallthrough count monotonically falls.",
        out_of_scope: "The resolution mechanism itself (namespace lane).",
        handback: "Fallthrough census, then the coverage receipt."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_4ELCVV2EIHCBGHMOG6T4IZEMT3", id: "declared-conformance-ground-fragment",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeSmall,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Declared conformance for the ground fragment — LANDED (gunbc#7484, merged 2026-08-01)",
        boundary: "ACCEPTED fragment, recut from floor-inhabitance-wall at its actual grain (operator spine verdict). fn returns (both arms, plus early returns stopping at lambda boundaries) and data annotations refuse non-conforming producers where BOTH sides are ground: kernel scalars, or Required non-keyed element collections of them — positive establishment, the four measured representation classes never guessed at. The counted unjudged advisory was EXCLUDED in final review scope: everything wider is byte-for-byte main behavior (silent), stated here so the fragment is never read as the class.",
        displaced_cost: "fn f() -> Int returning a string — the probe-3 specimen — refuses located instead of surfacing at the first consumer.",
        first_slice: "DONE — acceptance receipt: merged gunbc#7484; discriminating controls run against the prior binary.",
        red_control: "declared_type_conformance_witness — migrates to the probe corpus as this class's durable pair.",
        out_of_scope: "Everything the sibling nodes own; generic instantiation (record-construction lane).",
        handback: "Receipt recorded; residue on declared-conformance-grounding and declared-conformance-general-wall."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_WGRZFAYJ5EDVPNEQ42UAK7TD6D", id: "declared-conformance-grounding",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyHigh,
      volume: VolumeMedium,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Conformance grounding: the four representation classes stop being unjudgeable",
        boundary: "The measured false-positive classes that cap the ground fragment, each a §3 grounding defect not a checker defect: brand aliases unpeeled to their base; optionality living in two representations (return_cardinality vs the nominal Optional coproduct); anonymous record literals never grounded against their expected nominal; declaration-vs-body expansion depth. Ground each so the conformance relation widens class by class — the ground-fragment gate exists only because these are unjudgeable today.",
        displaced_cost: "Each grounded class moves thousands of silent declarations into the judged set (measured: the expansion-depth class alone was half the 3005-row frontier).",
        first_slice: "The brand-alias peel at conformance positions (the relation the method wall already built, second consumer).",
        red_control: "Per class: previously-unjudgeable correct code stays green AND a same-shape violation refuses — decidable in both directions or not claimed.",
        out_of_scope: "The general wall flip (next node); argument-position adjudication (its own node).",
        handback: "Classes grounded, frontier delta per class, probe receipts."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_E6PQ6WQR2J7SLMGBR62P3ECKGY", id: "declared-conformance-general-wall",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeMedium,
      t: fields(
        headline: "The general conformance wall: every grounded declared type constrains its producer",
        boundary: "As grounding lands per class, the conformance judgment widens to full return/data coverage — the gate dissolving into the relation until every grounded declared type refuses non-inhabiting producers, with whatever residue remains typed and counted, never silent.",
        displaced_cost: "Completes the keystone: a declared type is a contract everywhere, not per-fragment.",
        first_slice: "Widen to the first grounded class corpus-wide, census-adjudicated.",
        red_control: "The probe corpus's return/data pairs per class; corpus stays green as each class widens.",
        out_of_scope: "Argument positions (exemption lane); generic instantiation (record-construction lane).",
        handback: "The widened relation, residue census, probe receipts."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_EAOINVVBM732ZXS42ELVZAUPQV", id: "argument-type-compatibility-grounding",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeMedium,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Argument-type compatibility grounding: adjudicate what the exemption papers over",
        boundary: "module_skips_direct_call_arg_check exempts v2.*/v1.compiler.* from the argument TYPE judgment because of representation-gap false positives — the same four classes the conformance lane grounds, at the argument seam, plus the unlocated historical '104 TypeMismatch false positives' (no receipt found by two audits; adjudicate or refute it by measurement). Ground the argument-position relation so the exemption's reason dissolves.",
        displaced_cost: "The compiler's own sources are currently un-judged at every argument position — the largest single acceptance hole by module count.",
        first_slice: "Measure: run the check exemption-free in census mode, bucket every red by representation class.",
        red_control: "Each grounded class's argument-position probe pair; corpus reds adjudicated never exempted.",
        out_of_scope: "Deleting the exemption (its own node, gated on this one and conformance grounding).",
        handback: "The bucketed census, classes grounded, the 104-claim disposition."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_VEY66GYMNYZ24LWJQJGZGCFLRI", id: "floor-exhaustiveness-refusal",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyLow,
      volume: VolumeSmall,
      t: fields(
        headline: "ExhaustivenessUnknown refuses: the PatternLookupBlocked silent arm closes",
        boundary: "lookup_variant_in_type and lookup_field_in_variant answer PatternLookupBlocked with diagnostics: [] — exhaustiveness-not-established passing as success-adjacent. Split the verdict three ways (Exhaustive | NonExhaustive | ExhaustivenessUnknown) and refuse Unknown into any accepted executable artifact.",
        displaced_cost: "Closes the fallback-arm shape the census names for blocked lookups — exhaustiveness-not-established passing as success-adjacent; the measured disposition lives in the carrier, not this ticket.",
        first_slice: "The typed Unknown verdict plus the refusal, probe-paired with a blocked-lookup fixture.",
        red_control: "Probe: match whose coproduct lookup is blocked refuses as exhaustiveness-not-established; control: every resolved exhaustive match compiles.",
        out_of_scope: "PatternDynamic (already diagnoses); exhaustiveness algorithm changes for resolved types.",
        handback: "The verdict type, the two closed arms, probe flip receipt."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_P64CH3KXIZGL43SFS5DNJX52EQ", id: "floor-generic-field-constraint-wall",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeSmall,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Field access through an unconstrained generic refuses: delete the field_of_type_var fabrication",
        boundary: "field_of_type_var answers a field projection on a bare type variable by fabricating the field type — compile-time plausible output where no fact exists (the census's field-through-generic class). The wall: field projection on a type parameter with no field-carrying bound refuses with the parameter, field name, and locus; concrete receivers and parameters whose bound carries the field stay green.",
        displaced_cost: "A fabricated field type flows into inference and surfaces as a downstream mismatch or a wrong runtime value far from its cause; a located refusal moves the diagnosis to the projection site.",
        first_slice: "The refusal on the bare-parameter case with the concrete-receiver control green.",
        red_control: "The probe corpus's field-through-generic pair flips exactly when this lands; concrete-receiver and bounded-parameter controls never refuse.",
        out_of_scope: "A bounds/constraint language for generics (only the no-bound fabrication closes); where-refinement semantics.",
        handback: "The deleted fabrication arm, the refusal variant, the probe flip receipt."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_KPPUUSOXKTMKVJWBCW4G74ZP6A", id: "floor-method-ambiguity-wall",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeSmall,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Method ambiguity refuses: more than one resolution is a located error once primitive identity defines sameness",
        boundary: "The method-existence wall closes cardinality zero; this closes more-than-one — two distinct primitive identities (or a primitive and a user fn) resolving for one receiver/method pair refuse with both candidates named. Gated on primitive-identity-join because ambiguity is decidable only when sameness is: the length/count/size dispatch aliases make one method look like three today (the gunbc#7484 measured fork), so an ambiguity check before the join would refuse legitimate corpus or silently pick.",
        displaced_cost: "The silent-first-hit dispatch class: today arm order decides which of two candidates runs — an unstated tiebreak the census cannot even measure until sameness is defined.",
        first_slice: "The exactly-one check over the joined collection-algebra family, with the alias-reconciled controls green.",
        red_control: "A planted duplicate registration for one receiver/method pair refuses naming both candidates; every reconciled corpus call still resolves exactly-one.",
        out_of_scope: "Overload semantics by design (that would be a model change, not a tiebreak); the zero-resolution half (its own node).",
        handback: "The refusal variant, the duplicate-probe receipt, the exactly-one derivation site."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_LOVW74OSEOKAJHINOV2BVHPNCE", id: "cardinality-vertical-slice",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/cardinality-refinement.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyHigh,
      volume: VolumeMedium,
      t: fields(
        headline: "The operator's seam, end to end: a 0..n producer cannot feed a 1..n consumer",
        boundary: "One path, not a census: bare List = 0..inf, literal [] = 0..0, nonempty literal = n..n; map preserves, filter floors to 0, concat adds; the interval is an interface fact in InterfaceSummary's contract slot, actual-within-required enforced at function boundaries with a located seam refusal. The seam direction (2026-07-04) and candidate lattice exist; the in-tree fold-propagation rows are manual value-level specimens — binding-level propagation starts here. Construction-wall first candidate: type Refined<B> sole_constructor, which is why the sole-constructor completeness audit is a declared prerequisite edge (v2.std.refinement refined_vacuous_stub_pack, the forged Rejected-arm mint this candidate used to reference, is deleted outright — not merely fixed — as of the delete-first replacement in gunbc.std.refinement; the wall question below is unaffected and still open).",
        displaced_cost: "The canonical motivating specimen — simple, structural, explainable without compiler expertise; the first differentiating class an outside reader can verify.",
        first_slice: "The seam check on explicit intervals (no inference): producer-admits-zero into consumer-requires-nonempty refuses; proven-nonempty control compiles.",
        red_control: "The census's cardinality probe pair, plus filter-then-require-nonempty refusing unless a stronger proof intervenes.",
        out_of_scope: "The unwritable-seam construction wall beyond the first candidate; general refinement predicates (undecidable, permanently); width/overflow axes beyond the slice.",
        handback: "The lattice fragment landed, the seam judgment site, both probe receipts."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_PBIAB7X2M6IXIKMOXT3D7DKIXQ", id: "v2-self-grounding-frontier",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeMedium,
      t: fields(
        headline: "v2 self-grounding slice — LANDED (gunbc#7485, merged; acceptance receipt recorded 2026-08-01)",
        boundary: "ACCEPTED against its handback (operator spine verdict): exact self-evidence left solve_constraints' generic arm; underived facts are typed, located, counted GroundingNotDerived diagnostics inside an accepted InferredTree — the FrontierAccepted disposition's live specimen. Identity admission reads the authored declared-inhabitant roster, never caller-supplied candidates. The documented residue is the NEXT node's whole scope: Translate can still swallow the refusal and proceed.",
        displaced_cost: "Silent self-certification became a counted frontier: the deficit ranks for fixing instead of reading as green.",
        first_slice: "DONE — acceptance receipt: gunbc#7485 merged with the self-grounding and identity-admission witnesses enrolled.",
        red_control: "The claims carrier's v2 self-grounding path flips BelowFloor-to-FrontierAccepted exactly here; the identity path refuses caller-supplied candidate sets.",
        out_of_scope: "Translate propagation; carrier completeness; target realization (each its own node downstream).",
        handback: "The merged receipts and the frontier diagnostic counts by class."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_R34TEJZQSFSFZPHUPA3QLNDXYY", id: "v2-translate-underived-refusal",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeSmall,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Translate propagates the refusal: an underived fact cannot be swallowed downstream",
        boundary: "ACTIVE — the containment workstream, authorized to run parallel with the spine (operator spine verdict 2026-08-01: not another optional wall; it closes the one documented fail-open the merged frontier split created). gunbc#7485 records that Translate can swallow the new GroundingNotDerived rejection and continue — the frontier diagnostic exists but the emission path proceeds. Make Translate refuse or thread the typed frontier so Eval and Translate agree: compile-time refusal on both is the class minimum. The per-path grain is exactly why the carrier models paths separately.",
        displaced_cost: "Closes the path split where the same underived fact refuses in one phase and ships in another — the subject-grain failure mode measured on the call-shape class.",
        first_slice: "Translate refusing the existing frontier diagnostic, probe-paired with an underived-generic fixture.",
        red_control: "A source tree with an underived fact refuses translation naming the fact; every derived corpus module still translates.",
        out_of_scope: "New derivation rules; realization.",
        handback: "The refusal arm, probe flip, per-path disposition receipts."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_33MD6AG25ANERCNTXHLLCWSRAA", id: "v2-inferred-tree-completeness",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyHigh,
      volume: VolumeMedium,
      t: fields(
        headline: "InferredTree carries only derived facts: the all-derived carrier lands",
        boundary: "Separate source and inferred carriers so candidate-equals-source is not even well-typed as a grounding proof: every fact on the inferred carrier traces to a derivation or the node refuses. Branch/Match/Loop (the three real inference paths) migrate first; the validate_then_compile door and its lens roster stay. A well-formed node with no derived facts cannot inhabit the carrier.",
        displaced_cost: "InferredTree becomes a trustworthy proof boundary; every lens consuming it stops reading facts that were never derived; the self-host frontier stops reading greener than it is.",
        first_slice: "The carrier split with the three real inference paths migrated.",
        red_control: "A well-formed node with no derived facts cannot inhabit the inferred carrier (type-invalid, not lens-caught); the carrier's v2 disposition climbs exactly here.",
        out_of_scope: "Derivation rules beyond the three behaviors (next node); realization.",
        handback: "The carrier types, the migrated arm list, the disposition climb receipt."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_XYRCAJC6YWM4CU774LOSFYDJ4U", id: "v2-node-kind-derivation-coverage",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyHigh,
      volume: VolumeMedium,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Every node kind derives or refuses: the generic acceptance arm deletes",
        boundary: "The remaining derivation rules beyond Branch/Match/Loop: each v2 node kind either derives into the inferred carrier or its acceptance is a typed compile refusal — the generic accept-anything arm deletes. Coverage is counted per kind, so the frontier shrinks to zero or to named FrontierAccepted rows each carrying a trigger.",
        displaced_cost: "The last self-certification residue: any kind without a rule is currently accepted on well-formedness alone, which is the recovered defect class in its most general form.",
        first_slice: "The per-kind coverage census (derived | refused | frontier), then the highest-count kind's rule.",
        red_control: "A kind with neither rule nor refusal reds the coverage census; deleting the generic arm keeps the whole-tree compile green.",
        out_of_scope: "Realization; new language behaviors.",
        handback: "The per-kind coverage table and the deleted-arm commit."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_223FAUHF5IVK24UVR6PPYSXQCI", id: "v2-target-realization-gate",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyHigh,
      volume: VolumeMedium,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Realization per target: an operation cannot compile for T without exactly one realization",
        boundary: "The realized carrier adds target realization: every executable operation in a program accepted for target T has exactly one compatible realization row for T, refused target-relatively otherwise. gunbc#7485 explicitly leaves this open; it consumes the primitive-identity join (realization rows are its per-target facts) and the derivation-coverage node (a realized tree is derived-then-realized, never source-then-realized).",
        displaced_cost: "The gunbc#7479 shape at its root: a costed-but-unrealized primitive currently compiles and fails at dispatch; the gate moves that to a located target-relative refusal.",
        first_slice: "The gate over the collection-algebra family for the interpreter target, probe-paired.",
        red_control: "A costed-but-unrealized primitive refuses for the target naming the missing row; every realized corpus call still compiles.",
        out_of_scope: "New targets; deleting seed dispatch.",
        handback: "The gate site, the per-target refusal variant, probe flip receipt."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_VNYPK344GM56QEWP34G7VCG4OA", id: "floor-parse-formation-wall",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeSmall,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Parse formation refuses: a dropped separator cannot silently change the program",
        boundary: "Two slices, one wall. Safety: a missing list separator refuses at parse instead of parsing as element juxtaposition (the measured below-floor census row — a dropped comma silently changes list arity). Completeness: a block after a bare identifier in if-condition position parses as the block it is, closing the measured false refusal (expected-RParen on legitimate input). Probe-paired via the corpus's parser pair; grammar-owned, no host parser (census queue items 6-7).",
        displaced_cost: "The separator specimen survived regen, whole-corpus compile, fixed-point verify, and a 15-case matrix; only a human diff read caught it (review 45347).",
        first_slice: "The separator refusal with legitimate-list controls green.",
        red_control: "The separator probe flips exactly when the refusal lands; the if-block fixture parses correctly; every legitimate list in corpus still parses.",
        out_of_scope: "Grammar redesign; lookahead classes the census does not name.",
        handback: "The two closed defects, probe flips, corpus parse receipt."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_ILWLG34LVL5SAS6QPN5GZDPMFY", id: "floor-record-construction-wall",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeSmall,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Record construction refuses: missing required fields, bad defaults, ungrounded nominal literals",
        boundary: "A record literal missing a required field refuses at compile with the field named; defaults apply only where declared; a literal claiming a nominal type it does not ground refuses. Owns the census's record-completeness class — the declared-conformance chain owns return, data, and generic instantiation, not this. Probe-paired via the corpus's record-completeness pair. Motivating specimen: HandAuthoredDocBind's primary_work construction wall currently rests on record-completeness enforcement that is itself unmeasured.",
        displaced_cost: "A construction wall anywhere in the corpus is only as strong as required-field enforcement; this node is what makes primary_work-style walls load-bearing rather than declared.",
        first_slice: "Missing-required-field refusal, probe-paired.",
        red_control: "A record literal minus one required field refuses naming it; every corpus record literal compiles.",
        out_of_scope: "Row polymorphism; invocation default semantics (call-shape owns those).",
        handback: "The judgment site, probe flip, corpus receipt."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_6QXWDNSCBUAK6JWU7VSUWBXWMH", id: "accepted-obligation-door-mechanism",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyHigh,
      volume: VolumeSmall,
      t: fields(
        headline: "The acceptance door as mechanism: audit first, blocking later",
        boundary: "Split from the monolithic closure node (operator spine verdict: a door gated on the whole program delays the most important new mechanism until nearly done). This node lands the MECHANISM only, depending on the carrier alone: read every Required guarantee path, derive the missing/unmeasured/frontier/no-live-consumer census, run audit-mode and expecting-red — it reports, it does not yet block, and it never claims the open classes closed. The recovered P0.0 meta-guarantee gets its executable form here.",
        displaced_cost: "The every-Required-path-has-a-live-pre-Accepted-consumer relation becomes executable years before the last wall lands.",
        first_slice: "The closure fold over carrier rows with a synthetic Required-path-without-consumer RED.",
        red_control: "A Required path with no live consumer counts; a FrontierAccepted path admitted into Accepted counts; the audit totals reconcile with the carrier's row population.",
        out_of_scope: "Blocking (the two activation nodes); new walls.",
        handback: "The door site, the audit census, the RED receipts."
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_5FUBPPKWUGPBAYADIIIR3LDZKQ", id: "accepted-floor-obligation-closure",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
      intricacy: IntricacyMedium,
      volume: VolumeSmall,
      t: fields(
        headline: "Floor activation: the ordinary compiler floor flips to blocking",
        boundary: "The door mechanism flips from audit to refusal over the FLOOR domain only — names, call shape, conformance, fields, exhaustiveness, parse formation, record construction, the exemption gone: acceptance refuses when a floor class or path is Unmeasured, BelowFloor, FrontierAccepted, or lacks its live consumer.",
        displaced_cost: "Below-baseline safety regressions become unshippable — the floor stops depending on review vigilance.",
        first_slice: "Census-first over the floor domain (count, then flip), whole-tree green at flip.",
        red_control: "The mechanism's audit census reads zero over the floor domain before the flip; a planted floor violation refuses after it.",
        out_of_scope: "Extended domains (next node).",
        handback: "The flip receipt and the zero-census reading.",
      )
    ),
    active_sized(identity: "rn_FAF4MACL7ZXJMZ3GX6DJIR4E5S", id: "extended-admission-cardinality",
      owner: "compiler-guarantee",
      path: "docs/plans/compiler-guarantee-recovery-gap-analysis.md",
